  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Isostructural species are those which have the same shape and hybridization.</p><p>Number of election pair&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>]</mo></math><br />Where<br />V= Number of valence electron present in central atom<br />N=&nbsp;Number of non-monovalent atoms bonded to covalent atom<br />C= Charge of cation<br />A= Charge of anion</p><p>Hybridisation can be calculated by using this formula then we will be able to find the structure from hybridisation.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0166_d37c48b13ec5.png\" style=\"width: 374px; height: 827px;\" /></p>"
